# CODEOWNERS - who must approve changes to which files.
# Approval from code owners is only REQUIRED when "Require review from Code Owners" is switched on
# in your branch ruleset (see docs/branch-protection.md). This file must exist on the base branch.
# Later lines win over earlier ones. One approval from any listed owner is enough.
#
# Replace @your-org/maintainers and @your-username with real GitHub teams or users.
# Never list a bot or the Claude GitHub App as an owner.

# Default owner for everything
*                                   @your-org/maintainers

# The guardrails themselves: an agent must never be able to loosen these without a human
/.github/                           @your-username
/.claude/                           @your-username
/CLAUDE.md                          @your-username
/REVIEW.md                          @your-username
/docs/branch-protection.md          @your-username

# Build files that contain gate thresholds (coverage, SpotBugs, budgets, lint rules)
pom.xml                             @your-username
build.gradle                        @your-username
build.gradle.kts                    @your-username
package.json                        @your-username
angular.json                        @your-username
karma.conf.js                       @your-username
vitest.config.*                     @your-username
jest.config.*                       @your-username
eslint.config.*                     @your-username
.eslintrc*                          @your-username
lighthouserc.json                   @your-username
stryker.config.*                    @your-username
sonar-project.properties            @your-username

# Security-sensitive code (adjust paths to your project)
# /src/main/java/**/security/       @your-org/security
# /src/main/resources/db/migration/ @your-org/backend-leads
